---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Presentation deck" description="Interactive browser presentation with speaker notes for Workshop 1.">
<div class="container">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="eyebrow">Presenter mode · Workshop 1</div><h1>Presentation deck</h1><p>Use the arrow keys to navigate, open presenter notes for speaking guidance, or print the slides for a PDF handout.</p><div class="actions no-print"><button class="btn primary" id="print">Print / save PDF</button><a class="btn" href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL+'presenter/'}>Open presenter desk ↗</a></div></section>
  <section class="slide-shell" aria-live="polite"><div><div id="kicker" class="slide-kicker">MIS CLUB · WORKSHOP 1</div><h1 id="title">Build it. Version it. Ship it.</h1><div id="body"><p>Workshop 1 — Git &amp; GitHub</p><p>One three-hour session. One real portfolio. One repeatable development workflow.</p></div></div><div><div class="slide-controls no-print"><button class="btn dark" id="prev">← Previous</button><span id="count" class="slide-count">01 / 12</span><button class="btn primary" id="next">Next →</button></div><details class="notes no-print" open><summary>Presenter notes</summary><p id="notes">Welcome students. Set the expectation: the goal is not to memorize commands; it is to experience a safe, repeatable path from a change request to a live website.</p></details></div></section>
  <p class="muted small no-print">Keyboard: <span class="kbd">←</span> previous · <span class="kbd">→</span> next · <span class="kbd">P</span> print. On print, the current slide is emphasized; use presenter mode to navigate during a live session.</p>
</div>
<script>
const slides=[
{title:'Build it. Version it. Ship it.',body:'<p>Workshop 1 — Git &amp; GitHub</p><p>One three-hour session. One real portfolio. One repeatable development workflow.</p>',notes:'Welcome students. Set the expectation: the goal is not to memorize commands; it is to experience a safe, repeatable path from a change request to a live website.'},
{title:'Leave with something you can use.',body:'<ul><li>A personal portfolio in your own repository</li><li>A commit history and a reviewed pull request</li><li>A live GitHub Pages URL</li></ul>',notes:'Show the final result before teaching the tools. Connect this project to internships, applications, and future workshops.'},
{title:'From idea to published site.',body:'<p>Requirement → Issue → Branch → Edit → Commit → Pull request → Review → Merge → Deploy</p>',notes:'This is a simplified professional workflow. Later workshops add automated testing, security checks, and more structured AI development.'},
{title:'Git vs. GitHub',body:'<ul><li><b>Git:</b> tracks changes and versions in a project.</li><li><b>GitHub:</b> hosts repositories and adds collaboration features.</li><li><b>VS Code:</b> where we edit, inspect, and run the project.</li></ul>',notes:'Ask for an example of a tool versus a hosted service. Reinforce that Git can work locally without GitHub.'},
{title:'One project, with history.',body:'<p>A repository contains files plus their history. A commit is a named snapshot. A remote is a copy hosted elsewhere.</p>',notes:'Demonstrate the repository file list, README, commit history, and Source Control panel. Avoid a long command-line detour.'},
{title:'Three designs. One foundation.',body:'<ul><li>Editorial — warm, expressive, narrative-first</li><li>Developer — dark, technical, projects-first</li><li>Professional — structured and recruiter-friendly</li></ul>',notes:'Students choose the visual style; the repository structure and Git workflow remain consistent.'},
{title:'Ask. Inspect. Verify.',body:'<p>Ask Copilot to explain the project before editing. Request one small, focused change. Review the diff and preview the result before accepting it.</p>',notes:'Model a prompt with context, desired change, constraints, and acceptance criteria. Never paste credentials, tokens, or private data into prompts.'},
{title:'Define “done” before coding.',body:'<p>Example issue: “Add one featured project card.” Acceptance criteria: title, summary, link, and a responsive layout.</p>',notes:'Requirements make code review concrete. Ask students what evidence would show the feature is complete.'},
{title:'Keep changes small and named.',body:'<p>A branch isolates a piece of work. A commit records a useful checkpoint. Push sends commits to GitHub.</p>',notes:'Use the VS Code Source Control UI or terminal. Show the diff before staging and use a descriptive commit message.'},
{title:'A conversation about a change.',body:'<ul><li>Describe what changed and why</li><li>Compare the diff with acceptance criteria</li><li>Ask for feedback, then merge when ready</li></ul>',notes:'Even solo work benefits from a pull request as a review boundary. Ask students to inspect changed files before merging.'},
{title:'Publish the project.',body:'<p>GitHub Actions builds the Astro site and publishes static files. Check the Actions run and open the deployed URL.</p>',notes:'Repository settings and organization policy can affect Pages. A local preview is not proof the deployed base path and links are correct.'},
{title:'Keep building after today.',body:'<ul><li>Workshop 2: testing, Actions, and CI/CD</li><li>Workshop 3: secure development and DevSecOps</li><li>Workshop 4: spec-driven AI-assisted development</li></ul>',notes:'Exit check: each student shares a live URL, one Git concept, and one Copilot change they reviewed. The student remains accountable for AI-generated code.'}
];
let index=0;const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);function render(){const s=slides[index];$('title').textContent=s.title;$('body').innerHTML=s.body;$('notes').textContent=s.notes;$('kicker').textContent='MIS CLUB · '+String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')+' / WORKSHOP 1';$('count').textContent=String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')+' / '+String(slides.length).padStart(2,'0');$('prev').disabled=index===0;$('next').disabled=index===slides.length-1}$('prev').addEventListener('click',()=>{if(index>0){index--;render()}});$('next').addEventListener('click',()=>{if(index<slides.length-1){index++;render()}});$('print').addEventListener('click',()=>window.print());document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(e.target.closest('button,a,summary'))return;if(e.key==='ArrowRight'&&index<slides.length-1){index++;render()}if(e.key==='ArrowLeft'&&index>0){index--;render()}if(e.key.toLowerCase()==='p')window.print()});render();
</script>
</BaseLayout>